      "body": "1 Mayfair is a high-end residential building in London’s Mayfair district, comprising 29 luxury apartments arranged over a garden level, ground floor, seven upper storeys, and five basement levels. The lower floors accommodate extensive amenities including a gym, swimming pool, spa, and private parking, while the upper levels contain private residences with access to landscaped terraces and a central courtyard. The structure is designed with traditional stone façades and finely detailed elevations that reflect the architectural character of its historic surroundings, integrating modern construction methods with classical proportions and craftsmanship.\n\nBIM Technician, BIM Coordinator\n\nThe project required developing and managing a comprehensive BIM strategy for one of the most detailed and bespoke residential schemes undertaken by the studio. Initially, I joined the team as a BIM technician, supporting the main coordinator with modelling and coordination tasks. As the project evolved and its complexity deepened, I took over as the BIM Coordinator, leading the coordination process and guiding the digital delivery strategy. The scope covered numerous Revit models representing both internal and external elements of the building, alongside multiple consultant models, all managed within a unified, highly detailed environment.\n\nThe Model Samples\n\nClash Detection\n\nGeneral overview\n\nI led and automated the clash detection process using custom Dynamo scripts, streamlining over 150 multidisciplinary tests and ensuring seamless data flow between Revit, Navisworks, and Excel.\n\nModel federation and clash setup\n\nI federated architectural, structural, and MEP models in Navisworks, structured clash tests by trade and zone, and automated their setup and export for clarity and consistency.\n\nData feedback into Revit\n\nUsing custom workflows, I re-imported clash data into Revit to generate precise 3D views, enabling the design team to review and resolve issues directly within their models.\n\nFinal reporting\n\nThe generated 3D views were placed automatically onto sheets in Revit. These sheets were then exported as a high-quality PDF report, presenting coordination issues in a consistent, readable format.\n\nTeam Coordination & Advanced Modelling\n\nTeam Coordination\n\nI coordinate shell-and-core, fit-out, common-area and spa packages, providing modelling guidance and consistent data workflows. I also contribute to collaborative package guidance on model organisation, panelling parameters, tagging and reusable detail references.\n\nAdvanced Modelling\n\nI developed complex geometry through the Revit-Rhino Link, creating fabrication-ready components and supporting the translation of bespoke design intent into coordinated model information.",
