      "body": "King Street Townhouse in Manchester is a dedicated two-storey spa and leisure facility of approximately 822 m² located within a Grade II-listed Italian Renaissance building. The basement houses treatment rooms, a sauna, a lounge with access to a Himalayan salt cave, and dining facilities; above this level sits a state-of-the-art gym with cardio, free weights, functional training zones and a protein bar. The interior features a neutral palette with timber and stone finishes in the spa, and contrasts in the gym with industrial materials, dark colour schemes and bright way-finding lighting.\n\nTeam Support & Coordination\n\nThis project was particularly special to me, as it marked my very first experience as an independent BIM Coordinator. Although small in scale, it demanded a remarkable level of precision and sensitivity due to its refurbishment and interior design nature. Leading a compact team gave me the opportunity to shape our workflow, encourage collaboration, and develop my confidence in coordinating every digital aspect of the design process.\n\nMy role involved working with a detailed point cloud survey of the existing building, managing project phases, and supporting both architectural and interior design workflows.\n\nI contributed to bespoke model elements and high-quality visual presentations, ensuring consistency across documentation. I also carried out clash detection, monitored model health, and maintained a structured data environment to ensure smooth coordination between design disciplines.",
