      "links": [],
      "body": "Battersea Power Station Phase 3C is part of a major mixed-use development completing the southern end of Electric Boulevard. It delivers two residential buildings with 306 homes above a shared podium with gardens, along with retail space, a community hub, and extensive cycle and car parking. Designed to high sustainability standards, it features green roofs, enhanced public realm, and a target 10% biodiversity net gain, contributing to the wider regeneration of the Battersea Power Station masterplan. As Executive Architects, EPR continues to develop the concept into coordinated technical information.\n\nCoordination & Information Delivery\n\nBIM Coordination\n\nI lead coordination across the architectural, structural and MEP teams, managing clash workflows and the consistency of shared model information.\n\nGeometry & Technical Support\n\nI translate complex Rhino geometry into Revit for bespoke façade Support and structural elements. I support the technical team with modelling approaches and documentation, keeping the geometry usable within the project’s delivery workflow.\n\nInformation Delivery\n\nI contributed to Stage 3 BIM Execution Plan refinements and reviews of model packages against the agreed delivery structure. Ongoing work includes COBie room numbering, delivery responsibilities and package discrepancies as the project moves into Stage 4.",
