      "models": [],
      "links": [],
      "body": "Church Street Site A forms part of the wider regeneration of the Church Street neighbourhood. The scheme replaces outdated buildings with a residential-led mixed-use development, delivering new mixed-tenure homes, community and commercial space, and upgraded market infrastructure. It introduces publicly accessible open spaces, improved pedestrian and vehicle routes, and enhanced amenity areas to support local activity and wellbeing. The project is a key component of the area’s long-term renewal strategy, supported by a Compulsory Purchase Order to enable its implementation.\n\nBIM Coordination & COBie\n\nI support BIM delivery for Church Street Site A, maintaining architectural Revit models and coordinating information across the design team. The work connects model structure, project data and the client’s information requirements.\n\nA central focus is COBie preparation: defining the architectural asset scope, organising parameters and coordinating spatial references for future facilities management.\n\nI also prepare model inputs for clash review, investigate warnings and contribute to audit workbooks, turning findings into priorities for model improvement. The project and its information delivery remain ongoing.",
      "heroVideo": null,
      "videos": [],
