      "body": "At EPR, I connect parametric design, BIM and AI-assisted development. My work spans Dynamo and Python, Rhino-Revit interoperability and practical tools for coordination and information management.\n\nI support research into point-cloud workflows and embodied-carbon analysis, lead BIM-focused CPDs and contribute to the AI implementation group. The following pages bring these strands together with my pyRevit tools, C# Revit toolkit and independent software.\n\nParametric Balconies\n\nI developed parametric scripts and workflows to generate unique perforated balcony panels, with openings responding to building orientation, distance from a noisy street, and privacy / noise constraints.\n\nCPDs\n\nI led several CPD sessions focused on BIM, design software and emerging digital technologies.\n\nEmbodied Carbon Analysis\n\nI created an automated process to extract data from project models and feed Power BI dashboards, producing ready-to-use PDF reports for internal and external use, in collaboration with the sustainability team.",
