      "body": "The project explores the transformation of a prefabricated residential complex from the 1970s. Selective reduction of the existing mass is followed by extensions to the flats and a new layer of balconies and planting.\n\nThe study connects changes to individual homes with a wider site strategy, considering the building, its shared landscape and the details of the new façade.\n\ntutor: dr eng. arch. Magdalena Baborska-Narożny\n\nBalcony-Wall connection\n\n1. Structural Thermal Break Solution.\n\n2. Balcony slab support - steel tube 10/10 cm\n\n3. Balcony cover substructure - steel tubes 10/10 mm\n\n4. Balcony cover: - 2 mm thick anodized aluminium sheet\n\nExterior Wall\n\n1. Concrete column 40 cm\n\n2. Structural insulated panel 15 cm, between columns 30 cm.\n\n3. Façade substructure - steel tubes 10/10 mm\n\n4. Façade panels - 2 mm anodized aluminium sheet\n\nBalcony\n\n1. Balcony railing: - aluminium handrail 5/10 cm - steel fence net\n\n2. Balcony floor construction: - flower pot max. depth 24 cm - concrete slab - drainage system",
